{"kind":"request","text":"NF-1: make the client `Form` transport-neutral, and give the MCP field\nchecker one owner. One head with checker review and the gate.\n\nThis is the work of planner request 1a9330c2, which Hugh asked for in\na design review on 11 November. Read 1a9330c2 for the facts at main\ndf41e599, the five problems and the size estimate. It rests on order\nfc7576f8: the head removes a public export of\n`@generalbusiness/dap-client`, so it lands before the base freezes.\n\nScope, as 1a9330c2 states it.\n1. Move `actInputSchema`, `AT_INPUT`, `presentedSchema` and `schemaOf`\n   from packages/client/src/describe.ts to packages/mcp, beside\n   shape.ts.\n2. Remove `inputSchema` from `Form` and `target` from `FormContext`.\n   Add the declared `presents` and the `besideOf` flags to `Form`.\n   This revises the `formFor` contract of ruling 0be8be71.\n3. Delete the per-type `switch` in packages/mcp/src/shape.ts. MCP\n   forwards to the client's checker. The checker gains three options:\n   a member lookup for `@handle`, a text given by its digest, and a\n   pass for a platform mark. It reports a fault code with the field\n   path. MCP keeps its present wording in a table keyed by fault code.\n\nRulings.\n- `time`. The schema states the one form that `timeMs` accepts. Keep\n  `format: \"date-time\"`, add the pattern of `TIME` in\n  packages/bytes/src/ids.ts, and say in the description: UTC, ends in\n  `Z`, no fraction for whole seconds, otherwise three digits. This\n  changes two places in docs/mcp-tools.json. Report the change in\n  bytes of the tool list against the MCP budget.\n- `-0`. MCP refuses `-0` at the field path, as the kernel and the\n  client do. The change is wanted: today the value fails later in\n  canonical encoding with no path.\n- No other wording of an MCP refusal changes.\n\nNot in scope: `fitsFieldType`, `mostBytes`, `fieldAssignable`, the two\nparsers of a declared type, the room page's `Offered` builder, and the\ntyped fold over field types (request 5b2628b6, parked).\n\nOrder. After S4 9a053402 and after the identifier cutover head (c+d),\nbecause all three edit packages/mcp. Source work may start in its own\nlane when S4's MCP source is stable. No kernel file changes. The\nplanner deploys after the landing, and `MCP_ENABLED` stays off until\nS4 lands.\n\nWitnesses. A new `FieldType` case fails to compile in the MCP path.\nThe `-0` refusal names its field path. A `time` with an offset fails\nthe schema and the checker alike. The test that compares\ndocs/mcp-tools.json passes with only the two `time` places changed.","body":{"conditions":"Form has no inputSchema and FormContext has no target. packages/client holds no MCP envelope schema. packages/mcp/src/shape.ts has no per-type switch and forwards to the client's checker. MCP refuses -0 at the field path, and no other refusal wording changes. docs/mcp-tools.json changes only at the two time schemas, as ruled. npm run gate passes.","target_head":"df41e59964f09ce1d723ce870f5e4e5c6d8d4641","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}